.TH ROOT-MONITOR 1 "JAN 2026" "v1.0" "Root Users Project"
.SH NAME
root-monitor \- efficient process management and system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B root-monitor
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B root-monitor
is a lightweight process management utility. It provides a quick interface 
to monitor system load, identify resource-heavy tasks, and manage active 
processes through a simple command-line interface.
.PP
The tool reads user preferences from \fI/etc/root-monitor.conf\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List the top 10 processes. The sorting criteria (CPU or Memory) is 
determined by the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-search " \fINAME\fR"
Filter and display active processes whose names match the specified string.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kill " \fIPID\fR"
Terminate the process associated with the given PID using SIGTERM.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a concise summary of available commands.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/root-monitor.conf
.RS
System-wide configuration file.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP "root-monitor --list"
Display system activity sorted by default criteria.
.IP "root-monitor --search nginx"
Find all running instances of nginx.
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by the **Root Users Team** for the OS Lab Final Project.